[2026-03-15T23:24:24.057Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HAia7odVc3CgvT4bVUMD24","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Skill Reference\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It supports recording, uploading, and managing recordings through command-line operations.\n\n## Installation\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\nGenerate an API key from https://app.replay.io settings and set it as the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and begin recording at specified URL |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Upload recordings to Replay servers |\n| `list` | Display all local recordings with metadata |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete one or more recordings |\n| `login/logout` | Manage account authentication |\n| `info` | Show CLI version and browser details |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Upload source map files for debugging |\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n**Record a session:**\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\n```\n\n**Upload manually:**\n```sh\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\n## MCP Integration\nInstall the Replay MCP Server in Claude for advanced debugging capabilities using the provided configuration with your `REPLAY_API_KEY` authorization header.\n\nUse `-h` or `--help` with any command for additional options and details."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"69704494-380b-4838-ba19-18685fa812bd","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Skill Reference\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It supports recording, uploading, and managing recordings through command-line operations.\n\n## Installation\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\nGenerate an API key from https://app.replay.io settings and set it as the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and begin recording at specified URL |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Upload recordings to Replay servers |\n| `list` | Display all local recordings with metadata |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete one or more recordings |\n| `login/logout` | Manage account authentication |\n| `info` | Show CLI version and browser details |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Upload source map files for debugging |\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n**Record a session:**\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\n```\n\n**Upload manually:**\n```sh\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\n## MCP Integration\nInstall the Replay MCP Server in Claude for advanced debugging capabilities using the provided configuration with your `REPLAY_API_KEY` authorization header.\n\nUse `-h` or `--help` with any command for additional options and details.","durationMs":3815,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T23:24:24.058Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ERn558GChBmaX1ChDn23wr","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\nThis skill file documents **Replay MCP**, a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings that capture complete browser sessions. The file is organized into several key sections:\n\n## Core Purpose\n\"Use Replay MCP to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\" The tool functions as a detective instrument, allowing investigation of app behavior across time.\n\n## Key Concepts\nThe file introduces essential terminology:\n- **Points**: Specific execution moments when JS statements run or significant events occur\n- **Elements**: DOM element references independent of particular execution points\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what happened:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline tools (console messages, network requests, React renders, local storage)\n- Source tools (finding files, reading code, searching patterns)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking showing cause-and-effect relationships\n- Detail tools examining state, DOM elements, and variables\n\n## Investigation Methodology\nThe file recommends a structured approach: \"Frame your task in the form of a question that you need to answer,\" then use exploratory tools before forming hypotheses supported by gathered evidence.\n\n## Practical Guidance\nThe tips section emphasizes using the Logpoint tool to track expression values and exploring control dependencies to understand timing issues around events."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"66e96894-7b68-4d31-8957-04719495ca5b","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\nThis skill file documents **Replay MCP**, a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings that capture complete browser sessions. The file is organized into several key sections:\n\n## Core Purpose\n\"Use Replay MCP to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\" The tool functions as a detective instrument, allowing investigation of app behavior across time.\n\n## Key Concepts\nThe file introduces essential terminology:\n- **Points**: Specific execution moments when JS statements run or significant events occur\n- **Elements**: DOM element references independent of particular execution points\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what happened:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline tools (console messages, network requests, React renders, local storage)\n- Source tools (finding files, reading code, searching patterns)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking showing cause-and-effect relationships\n- Detail tools examining state, DOM elements, and variables\n\n## Investigation Methodology\nThe file recommends a structured approach: \"Frame your task in the form of a question that you need to answer,\" then use exploratory tools before forming hypotheses supported by gathered evidence.\n\n## Practical Guidance\nThe tips section emphasizes using the Logpoint tool to track expression values and exploring control dependencies to understand timing issues around events.","durationMs":3628,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
