[2026-03-15T23:24:33.976Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PXaYczDFSKbvU2VM5PAuEw","type":"tool_result","content":"1460-#### Test: Clicking a cycle navigates to cycle detail view\n1461-- **Initial state**: User is on `/team/eng-1/cycles` viewing the cycle list.\n1462-- **Action**: User clicks on the \"Sprint 2\" cycle row.\n1463:- **Expected**: The cycle detail view for \"Sprint 2\" is displayed, showing the cycle name, date range, progress stats, issue list, and burndown chart.\n1464-\n1465-#### Test: Cycle list shows empty state when team has no cycles\n1466-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, navigates to `/team/design-1/cycles`. The \"Design\" team has no cycles.\n--\n1478-#### Test: Clicking a different cycle after viewing one switches the detail view\n1479-- **Initial state**: User is on `/team/eng-1/cycles` and has clicked \"Sprint 2\" to view its detail.\n1480-- **Action**: User clicks back to the cycle list and clicks \"Sprint 1\".\n1481:- **Expected**: The detail view updates to show \"Sprint 1\" cycle information (name, date range, stats, issues, burndown chart). No stale data from \"Sprint 2\" is shown.\n1482-\n1483-### CycleDetail\n1484-\n--\n1530-\n1531-#### Test: Cycle detail renders correctly for a cycle with no issues\n1532-- **Initial state**: User views a newly created cycle \"Sprint 4\" that has no issues.\n1533:- **Expected**: The progress stats show \"Total: 0\", \"Completed: 0\", \"In Progress: 0\", \"Remaining: 0\". The progress bar is empty (0%). The issue list shows an empty state message (e.g., \"No issues in this cycle\"). The burndown chart shows no data.\n1534-\n1535-### CreateCycle\n1536-\n--\n1594-- **Expected**: The chart x-axis spans exactly from Jan 15 to Jan 28, matching the cycle's start and end dates. No dates outside this range are shown.\n1595-\n1596-#### Test: Burndown chart updates when an issue is marked as done\n1597:- **Initial state**: User is viewing cycle detail for \"Sprint 2\". The burndown chart shows 3 issues completed so far. Today is Jan 22.\n1598-- **Action**: User changes an issue's status from \"In Progress\" to \"Done\".\n1599:- **Expected**: The burndown chart updates to show an additional completion for today (Jan 22). The bar for today increases by 1. The total completions reflected in the chart match the updated progress stats.\n1600-\n1601-#### Test: Burndown chart shows empty state for cycle with no completed issues\n1602-- **Initial state**: User views cycle detail for a new cycle \"Sprint 4\" with 5 issues, all in \"Todo\" or \"Backlog\" status.\n1603:- **Expected**: The burndown chart renders with the correct date range but all bars at zero height (or an empty chart with a message like \"No issues completed yet\"). The chart axes and labels are still visible.\n1604-\n1605-#### Test: Burndown chart has readable axis labels and chart title\n1606-- **Initial state**: User views cycle detail for \"Sprint 2\" with completions on multiple days."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01QjYo4WQuKNMthcouqzzzPV","session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"bdb65ca7-faea-4af1-8aec-33d364b1725c"}
