orrect data for this cycle. Maybe the issue is that `fetchCycleIssues` succeeds but returns wrong dates. Since the cycle has no issues, the burndown should be empty but the dates should still generate all bars.\n\nActually, let me re-read `BurndownChart.tsx`:\n```tsx\nconst allDates = getAllDates(startDate, endDate);\n```\n\nThe `startDate` and `endDate` come from the cycle detail data. If the cycle-issues API returns correct dates, the chart should show all 28 dates.\n\nBut wait - what if the cycle-issues API fetch doesn't find the newly created cycle? The new cycle was created via API, but the test then navigates to the page and clicks on it. The `fetchCycleIssues` dispatch uses the `selectedCycleId` from Redux, which gets set when the cycle row is clicked.\n\nActually, let me look at what the `CycleDetail` component gets from Redux:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1329,"cache_read_input_tokens":149740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1329,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"98b4536c-85f9-4c0c-81f0-45d4228d6e75"}
