[2026-03-16T00:09:21.946Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01211o49ZZeJDbnhow26qtzA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Still 15. The clearing didn't help because: when `cycleDetail` is null, `ActiveCycle` renders `CycleList` instead of `CycleDetail`. The test waits for `cycle-detail` to be visible, which only appears when `cycleDetail` is non-null. So the flow is:\n\n1. Page loads, auto-selects Sprint 12, fetches its details → shows CycleDetail with Sprint 12\n2. Test clicks new cycle → `setSelectedCycleId(newCycleId)` clears cycleDetail → view switches to CycleList\n3. `fetchCycleIssues(newCycleId)` dispatches\n4. Test waits for `cycle-detail` which appears when fetch completes\n\nBut the test still sees 15 bars. This means the `fetchCycleIssues` for the new cycle actually returns 15 days. Let me check what's happening in the API.\n\nMaybe the `cycle-issues` API has a timing issue. Since the new cycle was just created, it should exist. But the `start_date` and `end_date` might be wrong.\n\nActually, wait. Let me look at the `createCycleViaApi` response more carefully. The POST response from cycles.ts is:\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"...\",\n  \"name\": \"...\",\n  \"startDate\": \"2026-08-01\",\n  \"endDate\": \"2026-08-28\",\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nBut the test uses `newCycle.id`. Let me check - does `createCycleViaApi` return the right structure?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":142,"cache_read_input_tokens":157784,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":142,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"8ce3f2d3-bfd0-4ffb-a909-7656464eb133"}
