[2026-03-16T00:09:33.490Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CgerMNhuW4giDyfQJ5Wo41","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The response from POST is the cycle object directly (not wrapped). So `newCycle.id` should work. The test then navigates to the page and clicks on `cycle-row-${newCycle.id}`.\n\nThe fact that we still see 15 bars means the chart is still showing Sprint 12's dates. Let me investigate by checking what happens when cycling - maybe the `cycle-detail` test ID appears before the new data loads due to a brief flash.\n\nActually, wait. I cleared cycleDetail in setSelectedCycleId. Now when the test clicks the new cycle:\n1. cycleDetail becomes null → CycleList shows (no cycle-detail)\n2. fetchCycleIssues dispatches\n3. When it completes, cycleDetail is set → CycleDetail shows with cycle-detail testId\n\nSo test waits for cycle-detail and should see the new cycle's data. But we're still getting 15.\n\nLet me add a wait for the cycle name to match:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":232,"cache_read_input_tokens":158671,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":232,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"c2c6ed88-6f38-446c-b2b9-28dd3cfd6d38"}
