[2026-03-16T00:10:44.467Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RgTFtPMuHXG9RXACcyyuzE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"So the detail still shows \"Sprint 12\" even after clicking the new cycle. The `setSelectedCycleId` clearing didn't work as expected - it clears `cycleDetail`, which hides the CycleDetail view, but then the auto-select effect fires again and re-selects Sprint 12.\n\nLet me trace the logic:\n1. Page loads → `fetchCycles` → cycles load (Sprint 12 is active) → auto-select Sprint 12 → `fetchCycleIssues(Sprint12)` → shows Sprint 12 detail\n2. Test clicks new cycle row → `setSelectedCycleId(newCycleId)` → clears cycleDetail → shows CycleList\n3. But wait - the `teamId` effect runs: `dispatch(setSelectedCycleId(null))` on mount... No, this only fires when teamId changes, not on cycle selection.\n4. `fetchCycleIssues(newCycleId)` dispatches via the effect\n5. But the auto-select effect also fires because `selectedCycleId` changed: `if (cycles.length > 0 && !selectedCycleId)` → `selectedCycleId` is the new ID (not null), so this doesn't trigger\n\nOK so the auto-select shouldn't re-trigger. But the cycle-detail is still showing Sprint 12. This means `fetchCycleIssues(newCycleId)` is either failing or returning Sprint 12's data.\n\nWait - maybe the issue is that when we clear `cycleDetail`, the `ActiveCycle` component stops rendering `CycleDetail` (shows CycleList instead). This means the test's `page.getByTestId('cycle-detail')` waits until `cycleDetail` is populated again. But the new `fetchCycleIssues` replaces `cycleDetail` with the new cycle's data...\n\nUnless the fetch fails! Let me check if the new cycle's ID is being used correctly. The test clicks `cycle-row-${newCycle.id}`, which calls `handleSelectCycle(newCycle.id)`. But maybe the cycle list doesn't include the new cycle (it was created via API, not through the UI flow, so `fetchCycles` might not have been called since creation).\n\nWait - the test navigates to the cycles page after creating the cycle. When the page loads, `fetchCycles(teamId)` is dispatched. If the fetch is fast, the new cycle should appear. But maybe there's a race condition.\n\nLet me check if the cycle row for the new cycle actually exists when the test tries to click it:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":392,"cache_read_input_tokens":159899,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":392,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"076c337b-1b48-4709-9430-a3fe1953e312"}
