[2026-03-16T00:11:01.796Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BmDadzz7gC6R1JJ89o6jgb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The page snapshot shows Sprint 12's detail view, meaning the click on the new cycle didn't change the view. The new cycle row might not exist in the list (the `cycle-row-${newCycle.id}` click might have silently failed or matched a stale element).\n\nActually, `page.getByTestId()` would throw if the element doesn't exist. But since we didn't wait for it... Let me check - the test does:\n```ts\nawait page.getByTestId(`cycle-row-${newCycle.id}`).click();\n```\n\nThis should fail if the element doesn't exist. But it doesn't throw - so the element exists.\n\nThe issue is that the click works, `handleSelectCycle(newCycleId)` dispatches, but the `fetchCycleIssues(newCycleId)` might fail (returning an error), so `cycleDetail` reverts to the previous state (Sprint 12). Let me look at how the Redux reducer handles the fetch:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":211,"cache_read_input_tokens":161974,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":211,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"28978b60-1bdb-4c41-8e34-4263ac20f854"}
