CASCADE` before CREATE to fix schema mismatch\n     - Wrapped index creation in `DO $ BEGIN ... EXCEPTION WHEN undefined_column OR undefined_table THEN NULL; END $` blocks\n\n   - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n     - Same CLI guard fix as schema.ts\n\n   - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`\n     - Fixed import: `import { devices as replayDevices, replayReporter } from '@replayio/playwright'`\n     - Added runtime detection of Replay Chromium availability (falls back to standard Chromium on aarch64):\n       ```ts\n       const replayChromiumAvailable = (() => {\n         try {\n           const config = replayDevices['Replay Chromium'];\n           if (!config?.launchOptions?.executablePath) return false;\n           const fs = require('fs');\n           return fs.existsSync(config.launchOptions.executablePath);\n         } catch { return false; }\n       })();\n       ```\n\n   - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/dev-server.ts` (NEW FILE)\n     - Custom dev server replacing `netlify dev` (which crashes on aarch64 due to Edge Functions/Deno)\n     - Loads all Netlify function handlers via dynamic import\n     - Starts Vite on port 5173, creates HTTP server on port 8888\n     - Routes `/api/*` to function handlers, proxies everything else to Vite\n     - CRITICAL: Uses `hostname: '::1'` for Vite proxy (Vite only listens on IPv6 on this system)\n     - Key code for function invocation:\n       ```ts\n       const fnReq = new Request(`http://localhost:${PORT}${url}`, {\n         method: req.method,\n         headers,\n         body: req.method !== 'GET' && req.method !== 'HEAD' ? body : undefined,\n       })\n       const fnRes = await handler(fnReq)\n       ```\n\n   - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/test.ts`\n     - Changed to use dev-server.ts instead of `netlify dev`:\n       ```ts\n       const netlifyDev = spawn('npx', ['tsx', 'scripts/dev-server.ts'], {\n         cwd: appDir,\n         env: { ...process.env, DATABASE_URL: ephemeralDbUrl, DEV_PORT: '8888' },\n         stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n         detached: true,\n       })\n       ```\n     - Updated server ready detection to look for \"Dev server ready\"\n     - Added broader process cleanup in killStaleProcesses\n\n   - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/cycles.ts`\n     - Fixed date formatting to handle Neon Date objects:\n       ```ts\n       const startStr = c.start_date instanceof Date ? c.start_date.toISOString().split('T')[0] : String(c.start_date).split('T')[0];\n       const endStr = c.end_date instanceof Date ? c.end_date.toISOString().split('T')[0] : String(c.end_date).split('T')[0];\n       ```\n\n   - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/cycle-issues.ts`\n     - Same date formatting fix for cycle dates, burndown dates, and issue due dates\n\n   - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/cyclesSlice.ts`\n     - Modified `setSelectedCycleId` to clear stale data:\n       ```ts\n       setSelectedCycleId(state, action: { payload: string | null }) {\n         if (state.selectedCycleId !== action.payload) {\n           state.cycleDetail = null;\n           state.cycleIssues = [];\n           state.burndown = [];\n           state.selectedIds = [];\n         }\n         state.selectedCycleId = action.payload;\n       },\n       ```\n     - Added ID check in fetchCycleIssues.fulfilled (CAUSED REGRESSION):\n       ```ts\n       .addCase(fetchCycleIssues.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n         if (action.payload.cycle.id === state.selectedCycleId) {\n           state.detailLoading = false;\n           state.cycleDetail = action.payload.cycle;\n           // ...\n         }\n       })\n       ```\n\n   - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/.env` (NEW FILE)\n     - Created from deployment.txt values\n\n   - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/node_modules/netlify-cli/dist/lib/edge-functions/proxy.js`\n     - Patched to not crash on Edge Functions setup failure (aarch64 incompatibility)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **schema.ts/seed-db.ts CLI execution on import**: Scripts had top-level `process.argv[2]` checks that ran when imported by test.ts. Fixed with `isMainModule` guards.\n   - **\"column member_id does not exist\"**: Production DB's sessions table had different schema. Fixed by dropping sessions table before recreation + wrapping index creation in exception-safe DO blocks.\n   - **replayDevices import error**: Export is `devices`, not `replayDevices`. Fixed import alias.\n   - **Replay Chromium x86_64 on aarch64**: Can't run. Made playwright config detect and fall back to standard Chromium.\n   - **Netlify CLI Edge Functions crash on aarch64**: Patched proxy.js, installed deno, still crashed. Then Netlify functions runtime itself had ECONNREFUSED. Solution: created custom dev-server.ts.\n   - **Vite IPv6-only listening**: Proxy to 127.0.0.1:5173 failed. Fixed by using `::1` as proxy hostname.\n   - **\"Invalid Date\" in cycle dates**: Neon returns Date objects, `String(date).split('T')[0]` doesn't produce ISO strings. Fixed with `instanceof Date ? .toISOString().split('T')[0]` pattern.\n   - **Race condition: 15 bars instead of 28**: Auto-selected Sprint 12's fetchCycleIssues completes after clicking new cycle, overwriting cycleDetail. Added clearing in setSelectedCycleId + ID check in fulfilled handler. **THIS CAUSED A REGRESSION from 6/7 to 3/7 passing.**\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved: Infrastructure issues (aarch64 compatibility, dev server, date formatting) - achieved 6/7 tests passing\n   - **ONGOING**: Race condition in cycle selection causing test 7 (\"long date range\") to show Sprint 12 data (15 bars) instead of new cycle data (28 bars). Last fix attempt (clearing cycleDetail + ID check) caused regression. Need to revert or adjust the approach.\n   - The best state achieved was **6/7 tests passing** (test-run-11 and test-run-12 before regression).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Initial task assignment: \"Read skill file: skills/tasks/build/testing.md. Subtasks to complete: 1. FixTests: 