[2026-03-16T00:15:09.453Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013FCmevjiPyz4z4FpDpT2f8","type":"tool_result","content":"   287→  test('Burndown chart handles a cycle spanning a long date range', async ({ page, baseURL }) => {\n   288→    const data = await loginViaApi(baseURL!, 'alice@acme.com', 'password123');\n   289→    const teams = await getTeams(baseURL!, data.token);\n   290→    const team = teams.find((t: { identifier: string }) => t.identifier === 'ENG');\n   291→\n   292→    // Create a cycle spanning 28 days (4 weeks)\n   293→    const cycleName = `Long Cycle ${Date.now()}`;\n   294→    const newCycle = await createCycleViaApi(\n   295→      baseURL!,\n   296→      data.token,\n   297→      team.id,\n   298→      cycleName,\n   299→      '2026-08-01',\n   300→      '2026-08-28'\n   301→    );\n   302→\n   303→    // Navigate to cycles page\n   304→    await page.goto('/login');\n   305→    await page.evaluate((t) => localStorage.setItem('session_token', t), data.token);\n   306→    await page.goto(`/team/${team.id}/cycles`);\n   307→    await expect(page.getByTestId('active-cycle-page')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n   308→    await expect(page.getByTestId('cycle-list')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n   309→\n   310→    // Click the long cycle\n   311→    await page.getByTestId(`cycle-row-${newCycle.id}`).click();\n   312→    await expect(page.getByTestId('cycle-detail')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n   313→    // Wait for the correct cycle to load (not the previously auto-selected one)\n   314→    await expect(page.getByTestId('cycle-detail-name')).toContainText('Long Cycle', { timeout: 15000 });\n   315→\n   316→    // Verify burndown chart renders\n   317→    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-chart')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 15000 });\n   318→    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-chart-container')).toBeVisible();\n   319→\n   320→    // Should have 28 bar columns for 28 days\n   321→    const barColumns = page.locator('[data-testid^=\"burndown-bar-\"]');\n   322→    await expect(barColumns).toHaveCount(28, { timeout: 15000 });\n   323→\n   324→    // Verify first and last date bars exist\n   325→    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-bar-2026-08-01')).toBeVisible();\n   326→    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-bar-2026-08-28')).toBeVisible();\n   327→\n   328→    // Verify x-axis labels are readable (some may be hidden for long ranges)\n   329→    // The chart uses showEveryNthLabel for label skipping on long ranges\n   330→    const visibleLabels = page.locator('.burndown-chart-x-label:not(.burndown-chart-x-label-hidden)');\n   331→    const visibleLabelCount = await visibleLabels.count();\n   332→    // For 28 days, should show fewer than 28 labels (label skipping active)\n   333→    expect(visibleLabelCount).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n   334→    expect(visibleLabelCount).toBeLessThanOrEqual(28);\n   335→  });\n   336→});"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"83a5d278-8eb4-4758-8c26-b9c406a4f444","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/burndown-chart.spec.ts","content":"  test('Burndown chart handles a cycle spanning a long date range', async ({ page, baseURL }) => {\n    const data = await loginViaApi(baseURL!, 'alice@acme.com', 'password123');\n    const teams = await getTeams(baseURL!, data.token);\n    const team = teams.find((t: { identifier: string }) => t.identifier === 'ENG');\n\n    // Create a cycle spanning 28 days (4 weeks)\n    const cycleName = `Long Cycle ${Date.now()}`;\n    const newCycle = await createCycleViaApi(\n      baseURL!,\n      data.token,\n      team.id,\n      cycleName,\n      '2026-08-01',\n      '2026-08-28'\n    );\n\n    // Navigate to cycles page\n    await page.goto('/login');\n    await page.evaluate((t) => localStorage.setItem('session_token', t), data.token);\n    await page.goto(`/team/${team.id}/cycles`);\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('active-cycle-page')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('cycle-list')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n\n    // Click the long cycle\n    await page.getByTestId(`cycle-row-${newCycle.id}`).click();\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('cycle-detail')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n    // Wait for the correct cycle to load (not the previously auto-selected one)\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('cycle-detail-name')).toContainText('Long Cycle', { timeout: 15000 });\n\n    // Verify burndown chart renders\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-chart')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 15000 });\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-chart-container')).toBeVisible();\n\n    // Should have 28 bar columns for 28 days\n    const barColumns = page.locator('[data-testid^=\"burndown-bar-\"]');\n    await expect(barColumns).toHaveCount(28, { timeout: 15000 });\n\n    // Verify first and last date bars exist\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-bar-2026-08-01')).toBeVisible();\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-bar-2026-08-28')).toBeVisible();\n\n    // Verify x-axis labels are readable (some may be hidden for long ranges)\n    // The chart uses showEveryNthLabel for label skipping on long ranges\n    const visibleLabels = page.locator('.burndown-chart-x-label:not(.burndown-chart-x-label-hidden)');\n    const visibleLabelCount = await visibleLabels.count();\n    // For 28 days, should show fewer than 28 labels (label skipping active)\n    expect(visibleLabelCount).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n    expect(visibleLabelCount).toBeLessThanOrEqual(28);\n  });\n});","numLines":50,"startLine":287,"totalLines":337}}}
[2026-03-16T00:15:30.093Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YXAXpLckA648eYSgb29WN1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test already waits for `cycle-detail-name` to contain 'Long Cycle'. The issue is that even after the correct cycle name shows, the burndown bars may still show the old cycle's data until the cycle-issues API response for the new cycle arrives and re-renders.\n\nThe race condition: when the page loads, it auto-selects the first cycle and fetches its data (15 bars for Sprint 12). Then the test clicks the new cycle, which triggers a new fetch. But the old fetch response might arrive after the new fetch started, overwriting the data.\n\nActually wait - I reverted the Redux changes, so now `fetchCycleIssues.fulfilled` always updates regardless of which cycle is selected. \n\nThe real problem is that the initial fetch for the first cycle completes after the new cycle's fetch, so it overwrites the 28 bars with the old 15 bars.\n\nI could fix this in the Redux slice by properly checking the cycle ID before updating, but that caused regressions in tests 4-7 where the DOM elements weren't found or the login failed. Alternatively, I could make the test wait for the race condition to settle, or ensure it waits for the specific API response before asserting on the new cycle data. with 500 errors - that's a server issue, not related to the Redux change. Tests 4 and 5 failed because `cycle-detail` / `cycle-list` weren't visible.\n\nSo actually the 500 errors in tests 6 and 7 are probably transient server issues (maybe the DB was under load from the previous tests creating cycles). The Redux change may have only caused test 4 to fail.\n\nLet me think about test 4 more carefully. It creates a new empty cycle, navigates to cycles page, clicks the cycle row - but `cycle-detail` never becomes visible. The ID check in the fulfilled handler means: if the cycle list auto-selects a different cycle and fetches its issues, that fetch completes but gets rejected because it doesn't match `selectedCycleId`. Then when the test clicks the new cycle, `setSelectedCycleId` clears `cycleDetail`, and dispatches a new `fetchCycleIssues`. When that completes, it checks if the cycle ID matches the currently selected one - which should be true since we just set it.\n\nBut maybe the component only renders `cycle-detail` when it's non-null in the state. Let me trace through what actually happens when clicking a cycle row - does it set the selected ID and then fetch, or is there something else going on?","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1120,"cache_read_input_tokens":37102,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1120,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"dd216148-a227-4eac-b51c-302b45a58728"}
