[2026-03-16T00:16:42.507Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CF6RmV9oyBjYmtai7wajdb","type":"tool_result","content":"   192→  test('Burndown chart shows empty state for cycle with no completed issues', async ({ page, baseURL }) => {\n   193→    const data = await loginViaApi(baseURL!, 'alice@acme.com', 'password123');\n   194→    const teams = await getTeams(baseURL!, data.token);\n   195→    const team = teams.find((t: { identifier: string }) => t.identifier === 'ENG');\n   196→\n   197→    // Create a new empty cycle via API\n   198→    const cycleName = `Empty Chart Cycle ${Date.now()}`;\n   199→    const newCycle = await createCycleViaApi(baseURL!, data.token, team.id, cycleName, '2026-07-01', '2026-07-14');\n   200→\n   201→    // Navigate to cycles page\n   202→    await page.goto('/login');\n   203→    await page.evaluate((t) => localStorage.setItem('session_token', t), data.token);\n   204→    await page.goto(`/team/${team.id}/cycles`);\n   205→    await expect(page.getByTestId('active-cycle-page')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n   206→    await expect(page.getByTestId('cycle-list')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n   207→\n   208→    // Click the new empty cycle\n   209→    await page.getByTestId(`cycle-row-${newCycle.id}`).click();\n   210→    await expect(page.getByTestId('cycle-detail')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n   211→\n   212→    // Verify burndown chart shows empty state\n   213→    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-chart')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 15000 });\n   214→    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-chart-empty')).toBeVisible();\n   215→    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-chart-empty')).toContainText('No issues completed yet');\n   216→\n   217→    // Chart container and axes should still render\n   218→    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-chart-container')).toBeVisible();\n   219→  });"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"abc9424d-1cdc-458d-a4cb-fbdc65a7951f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/burndown-chart.spec.ts","content":"  test('Burndown chart shows empty state for cycle with no completed issues', async ({ page, baseURL }) => {\n    const data = await loginViaApi(baseURL!, 'alice@acme.com', 'password123');\n    const teams = await getTeams(baseURL!, data.token);\n    const team = teams.find((t: { identifier: string }) => t.identifier === 'ENG');\n\n    // Create a new empty cycle via API\n    const cycleName = `Empty Chart Cycle ${Date.now()}`;\n    const newCycle = await createCycleViaApi(baseURL!, data.token, team.id, cycleName, '2026-07-01', '2026-07-14');\n\n    // Navigate to cycles page\n    await page.goto('/login');\n    await page.evaluate((t) => localStorage.setItem('session_token', t), data.token);\n    await page.goto(`/team/${team.id}/cycles`);\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('active-cycle-page')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('cycle-list')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n\n    // Click the new empty cycle\n    await page.getByTestId(`cycle-row-${newCycle.id}`).click();\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('cycle-detail')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n\n    // Verify burndown chart shows empty state\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-chart')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 15000 });\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-chart-empty')).toBeVisible();\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-chart-empty')).toContainText('No issues completed yet');\n\n    // Chart container and axes should still render\n    await expect(page.getByTestId('burndown-chart-container')).toBeVisible();\n  });","numLines":28,"startLine":192,"totalLines":337}}}
[2026-03-16T00:16:53.426Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01443sU1JteiwVn8W7ZHqFjy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Test 4 failed at line 210: `cycle-detail` not found. The test clicks `cycle-row-${newCycle.id}` at line 209 but the detail never becomes visible. \n\nWith the ID check (but no clearing), when the page loads:\n1. Auto-selects first cycle → dispatches fetchCycleIssues(firstCycleId)\n2. fetchCycleIssues(firstCycleId) completes → sets cycleDetail to first cycle's data\n3. CycleDetail becomes visible with first cycle's data\n4. Test clicks new cycle → dispatches setSelectedCycleId(newCycleId) \n\n\n5. useEffect triggers fetchCycleIssues(newCycleId)\n6. fetchCycleIssues(newCycleId) completes → ID matches → updates cycleDetail\n\nSo cycle-detail should stay visible throughout, just switching from the first cycle's data to the new one. The ID check shouldn't be hiding it. I'm wondering if the new cycle's ID isn't actually in the cycle list—maybe it was created via API but the page's cycle list was fetched before that happened. Though the test navigates to the page after creating the cycle, so fetchCycles should pick it up.\n\nActually, I'm realizing those 500 errors from the previous test run might've been from the login endpoint rather than anything to do with the Redux changes, and tests 4 and 5 could've failed for unrelated reasons. Let me just run the tests as they are now with the ID check in place but without clearing, and see what actually happens.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":735,"cache_read_input_tokens":43502,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":735,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"00774acd-f44b-447f-b785-b149b6d94a3f"}
