[2026-03-16T00:21:28.986Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Y7TJxptz92NvJss4fhbNQ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the issue! Look at lines 108-117 of ActiveCycle.tsx:\n\n```jsx\n{selectedCycleId && cycleDetail ? (\n  <CycleDetail />\n) : (\n  <CycleList ... />\n)}\n```\n\nWhen `selectedCycleId` is set AND `cycleDetail` is truthy, it renders `CycleDetail` and HIDES `CycleList`. When `cycleDetail` is null, it shows `CycleList`.\n\nNow look at the auto-selection flow:\n1. Page loads → fetchCycles → cycles load\n\n\n2. Auto-selects active cycle → `setSelectedCycleId(activeCycleId)` → `selectedCycleId = activeCycleId`\n3. useEffect triggers `fetchCycleIssues(activeCycleId)`\n\nDuring step 3 (fetch is in-flight), `cycleDetail` is null, so `CycleList` is shown. Good - the test can see and click cycle rows.\n\n4. Test clicks new cycle row → `setSelectedCycleId(newCycleId)` → `selectedCycleId = newCycleId`\n5. useEffect triggers `fetchCycleIssues(newCycleId)` - but here's the problem: while this fetch is in-flight, `cycleDetail` is still the old data from step 3, so the condition `selectedCycleId && cycleDetail` is true and `CycleDetail` stays visible instead of switching back to `CycleList`.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the race condition where the first fetch completes before the user clicks. If `fetchCycleIssues(activeCycleId)` finishes before step 4, then `cycleDetail` gets populated, and when the user clicks the new cycle, the old detail view persists while the new fetch loads. So the click succeeded, but then the cycle detail never showed up. That's strange—if `selectedCycleId` changed after the click, the fetch should have been triggered and `cycleDetail` should populate once it completes. Unless the API call is failing silently without setting any error state. Let me trace through the auto-selection logic to see if there's something I'm missing about how the initial cycle gets selected.\n\nWhen the component first mounts and the team changes, `selectedCycleId` gets reset to null. Then once the cycles list loads, the auto-selection effect should kick in and pick the active cycle. But the click handler is also trying to select a cycle manually. The issue might be that the auto-selection is interfering with the manual selection, or the fetch for the newly selected cycle is failing without any visible error. Tests 1-3 pass using `loginAndGoToCycleDetail`, which fetches cycles, navigates to the page, waits for the cycle list, then clicks and views a specific cycle. Test 4 creates a new cycle and follows the same flow, but fails at the cycle-detail step—likely because the auto-selection logic is interfering between waiting for the cycle list and clicking the new cycle row.\n\nThe click itself succeeds (error is later), so the element was in the DOM. What's probably happening is the click sets the selected cycle ID, triggering a fetch for that cycle's issues, while the auto-selection effect is also pending from the fresh cycle load. Since the selected ID is now set, auto-selection gets skipped, and the fetch completes to populate the cycle detail. I'm tracing through the effect chain to see if something's overriding the manual click. When the page mounts, it sets selectedCycleId to null, then fetchCycles runs. Once cycles load, there's a check for an active cycle—if none exists, selectedCycleId stays null and the list remains visible instead of showing the detail view.\n\nThe race condition is clear now: if the auto-selection effect runs after the test clicks, it overwrites the newCycleId with the activeCycleId, triggering fetchCycleIssues for the wrong cycle. The test's click gets lost in the effect ordering.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5840,"cache_read_input_tokens":57002,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5840,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"out