e fetch for the new cycle has already completed before the test even checks the results.\n\nLet me trace through what happens when the cycle is created via the API. The test calls `createCycleViaApi`, which makes a POST request to the cycles endpoint and returns the full response object with the cycle data.\n\nWhen `fetchCycleIssues` is called with that cycle ID, it queries the cycle-issues endpoint. If the cycle doesn't exist in the database at that point, the request would fail and `cycleDetail` would remain null. I should check whether the cycle-issues endpoint is actually finding the cycle that was just created, or if there's a timing issue where the cycle hasn't been persisted yet.\n\nLooking at the test snapshot more carefully, the cycle list shows \"Sprint\" as the only entry, which suggests the newly created cycle might not be appearing in the list at all. I need to trace through what's happening when the request is made. The rejected handler would set an error, but nothing's showing up in the UI. Let me check if there's a routing issue on the dev-server side—maybe the cycle-issues endpoint isn't wired up correctly to its handler.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6272,"cache_read_input_tokens":62842,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6272,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"f7366d53-10ff-4d78-be90-2e4574657843"}
