ect Long Cycle instead of relying on UI clicks.\n\nThe Redux store isn't exposed on window though, so dispatching actions that way won't work. A simpler solution is to navigate to a neutral route first like `/my-issues` to reset the Redux state, then navigate back to cycles. Or even more straightforward: just reload the page and wait for everything to settle before clicking the cycle row.\n\nBut there's still a race condition—the cycle list stays visible until Sprint 12's fetch completes, so the test waits for it to appear, then clicks Long Cycle. Meanwhile Sprint 12's fetch is also running, and both responses race to update the state. The reload helps a bit because Sprint 12's fetch might finish before the test clicks, which would hide the cycle list and prevent the click. The most reliable fix is to use `page.route` to deliberately delay Sprint 12's response so Long Cycle's response arrives last and overwrites the state.\n\nIntercepting the API response...\n\nActually, I need to flip the delays—Long Cycle should have the longer delay so its response arrives last, not first. any filtering, the last response to arrive wins (overwrites). So I want Long Cycle's response to be the last one. I should delay the Long Cycle's response MORE than Sprint 12's. But that means Sprint 12's data would show first, then be overwritten by Long Cycle's. That's what I want!\n\nWait no - the issue is the OPPOSITE. Sprint 12's response arrives LAST and overwrites. I want Sprint 12's response to arrive FIRST, and Long Cycle's to arrive LAST (so it overwrites Sprint 12's data).\n\nSo I should delay Sprint 12's response LESS (let it arrive quickly) and the Long Cycle response MORE (let it arrive last). But that doesn't help because Sprint 12's response ALREADY arrives first in many cases. The problem is when it arrives LAST.\n\nI need Sprint 12's response to arrive BEFORE the Long Cycle's. I'm setting up a route handler that intercepts the Long Cycle API call and adds a 2-second delay before fulfilling it, ensuring Sprint 12's response comes through first and then gets overwritten by Long Cycle's data when it finally arrives.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":840,"cache_read_input_tokens":159626,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":840,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"94f898e6-35fd-464e-89c5-15d3496e8466"}
