[2026-03-16T01:13:35.938Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SgUHHBu84Kuq8eGfx3V32o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The page snapshot shows the cycle list is visible with:\n- Sprint 12 (Active)\n- Empty Chart Cycle (active/selected button state)\n\nSo the CycleList IS visible. The \"Empty Chart Cycle\" button has `[active]` attribute, meaning it was clicked. But CycleDetail never appeared.This means: the click on `cycle-row-${newCycle.id}` happened (the button shows as active). But `cycleDetail` remained null, so `selectedCycleId && cycleDetail` stayed falsy, and CycleList kept rendering.\n\nSo `selectedCycleId` is set to the new cycle's ID (because the button was clicked). \n\nBut `cycleDetail` is still null, which suggests the fetch was dispatched but the response got filtered out. If auto-selection switched back to Sprint 12 between the click and when the response arrived, then the ID check would reject the new cycle's data since the selected ID no longer matches what was requested.\n\nThe teamId effect resets `selectedCycleId` to null on mount or when the team changes, which could trigger auto-selection. I'm wondering if there's a component remount happening during navigation to `/team/${team.id}/cycles`, or if the click on the cycle row happens before the component has fully initialized.\n\nActually, I think I see the issue now. The sequence is: cycles load and auto-selection sets `selectedCycleId` to Sprint12, then `fetchCycleIssues(Sprint12)` starts. When the test clicks the Empty Cycle, it sets `selectedCycleId` to EmptyCycleId and dispatches `fetchCycleIssues(EmptyCycleId)`. But then the Sprint12 response arrives with `meta.arg=Sprint12` while `selectedCycleId` is now EmptyCycleId, so it gets skipped. The question is what happens when the EmptyCycle response arrives—does `selectedCycleId` still match? What if between step 5 and step 6, something changed selectedCycleId?\n\nActually, let me check if there's a re-render that causes the fetchCycleIssues effect to fire again. The effect depends on [selectedCycleId, token, dispatch]. After step 3, selectedCycleId changed to EmptyCycleId, so the effect fires fetchCycleIssues(EmptyCycleId) in step 4.\n\nBut wait, step 2 already dispatched fetchCycleIssues(Sprint12). In step 5, that response arrives. The fulfilled handler returns early. state doesn't change. No re-render. Then in step 6, EmptyCycle response arrives. meta.arg=EmptyCycleId, state.selectedCycleId=EmptyCycleId. They match! cycleDetail gets set and CycleDetail renders.\n\nThis should work, so something else is going on. Maybe the newly created cycle doesn't have any issues data and the API call is failing instead of succeeding. Let me check what the cycle-issues endpoint actually returns for a fresh cycle.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1132,"cache_read_input_tokens":67148,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1132,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"f0206a50-d285-4946-b03c-422250025f91"}
