eId it's seeing at that point.\n\nI could use page.route to intercept the API calls directly in the test, or I could add a condition callback to createAsyncThunk to prevent duplicate dispatches...\n\nAdding condition callback to thunk...\n\nActually, that would block refetching which breaks the other test. Let me revert the ID check and instead use page.route to intercept and delay Sprint 12's response so the timing works out correctly.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4037,"cache_read_input_tokens":74168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4037,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"e07a062b-8e14-447e-acf3-a1f96547fdb1"}
