re, so the SQL should behave identically.\n\nWait, I should verify whether the Long Cycle is even persisted to the database by the time the API call tries to fetch it. The test creates the cycle via POST to the dev server, which writes to the Neon ephemeral branch, then immediately tries to read it back. Since both operations hit the same database endpoint, that should work fine. But I'm noticing that `resetDatabase` runs before all tests, and then state accumulates between them—test 4 creates an empty cycle first, then test 7 creates the Long Cycle. The cycles endpoint should handle multiple cycles without issue though, so that's probably not it either.\n\nLet me add better error capture to see what's actually happening. I'm already logging the generic \"Internal server error\" response, but the real error details are being logged to the dev server's console, which isn't visible in the test output. I should modify the test to inspect what `newCycle.id` actually contains or check if the response format is different than expected.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4973,"cache_read_input_tokens":104181,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4973,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1880e500-2182-4a27-9a5d-5f74c5e8203c","uuid":"6c1fc245-eb52-4040-8f0a-a9a57b47c2db"}
